summary is: {{ SOAP Note: 
Subjective: 
Patient presented with diarrhea for three days, which started with vomiting, and now just diarrhea. He has been going to the toilet five to six times a day, with watery stools, no blood in stools, no abdominal pain, and feels dehydrated. He has not been able to eat solids, feels weak, and has a little bit of temperature.
Objective: 
No physical examination was performed.
Assessment: 
Patient is suffering from gastroenteritis, which is an infection of the gut. He has a viral gastroenteritis, which is self-limiting and usually lasts for three to five days.
Plan: 
Patient is advised to drink plenty of fluids to flush out the toxins and replace lost electrolytes. He can take Dioralyte and Paracetamol for fever and weakness. He is advised to take time off work for the next day or two until he recovers. If he is not better in a week, he should come back and see the doctor. He is also advised to take plenty of rest and to avoid solid food until his symptoms improve. }}<|eot_id|>
