summary is: {{ SOAP Summary

Subjective: The patient, a 40-year-old female, presents with a 2-hour history of dizziness, feeling of the room spinning, and ear buzzing. She has also experienced nausea and vomiting. She has had similar episodes in the past, but this episode has lasted longer than usual.

Objective: The patient's temperature is not reported, but she is not pyrexial. She is feeling unwell and has a headache. She is not experiencing any ear pain or discharge.

Assessment: The patient's symptoms are consistent with labyrinthitis, which is an inflammation of the inner ear. This is causing her symptoms of dizziness and nausea.

Plan: The patient will be prescribed medication to help alleviate her symptoms. She will also be seen by a doctor to examine her ears and assess her condition. If her symptoms worsen or she experiences any new symptoms, she will be advised to seek immediate medical attention.

Doctor's Note: The patient will be prescribed a 10-day course of medication to help alleviate her symptoms. She will be seen by a doctor to examine her ears and assess her condition. She will also be advised to take her medication as directed and to seek immediate medical attention if her symptoms worsen or she experiences any new symptoms. }}<|eot_id|>
