summary is: {{ SOAP Note:
Patient: Barbara
Age: 38
Chief Complaint: Diarrhea and vomiting
Duration: 3 days
History of Present Illness: Barbara has had diarrhea and vomiting for the past 3 days. She has had loose stools and has been vomiting everything she takes, including water. She has not been able to keep anything down and has not been able to urinate in the past 24 hours. She has had a high temperature and has been feeling feverish. She has also had abdominal pain and has been unable to touch her navel area. She has not had any blood in her stool or urine. She has not had any episodes of diarrhea or constipation before.

Past Medical History: She has had no previous medical problems and has never been hospitalised before. She has had a normal diet and does not smoke or drink alcohol.

Social History: She is a graphics designer and works from home. She lives with her brother and mother. She has not been abroad recently and has not had any recent contact with anyone who has had similar symptoms.

Physical Examination: She is unwell and looks pale. She has a high temperature and is shivering. She has abdominal tenderness and is unable to touch her navel area. She is dehydrated and has not passed urine in the past 24 hours.

Plan: She will be seen in the clinic for further assessment and treatment. She will be given rehydration salts to drink and will be advised to have small amounts of simple food such as toast or biscuits. She will be given antibiotics if her symptoms do not improve. She will also be advised to keep drinking small amounts of water and to avoid anything that makes her symptoms worse. She will be seen in the clinic within the next 24 hours. }}<|eot_id|>
