summary is: {{ SOAP (Subjective, Objective, Assessment, Plan) Summary:
 
Subjective: The patient, Sarah Smith, a 38-year-old female, is a new mother who had a C-section four weeks ago. She is experiencing shortness of breath for the last hour, which is getting worse. She has also had a cough for the last day and is feeling stressed and anxious. She is worried about her heart and has noticed it is beating rapidly. She has had a C-section and is allergic to Ibuprofen.

Objective: The patient has no chest pain and is not coughing up blood. She has not had any recent medication and has not taken any Ibuprofen. She has not had any fever or chills. She is not having any difficulty breathing when lying flat, but is short of breath when sitting up.

Assessment: The patient is experiencing shortness of breath and is worried about her heart. She has had a C-section and is allergic to Ibuprofen. She has no chest pain or coughing up blood. She is not having any difficulty breathing when lying flat, but is short of breath when sitting up. She is worried about her heart and has noticed it is beating rapidly.

Plan: The patient is advised to take herself to the hospital with baby to be checked out further. She is advised to take some bits for baby at the same time and not to take any medications like Codeine. The doctor is worried about the possibility of a pulmonary embolism, which is a blood clot in the lungs. She is advised to go to the hospital and get checked out further. }}<|eot_id|>
